 "title": "15° is half of 30°",
 "caption": "cos²15° = (1 + cos 30°)/2 = (2 + √3)/4. The point at 15° is acute, so its x-coordinate is positive: cos 15° = √(2 + √3)/2 = (√6 + √2)/4 ≈ 0.966.",
